I'll investigate the current move implementation and the file explorer UI.Let me look at the file-finder API and its UI components.Let me read the FileFinder component and locate its API module.Let me inspect the actual file-browser folder structure on disk.The search index appears stale. Let me read the actual API module and check how it's wired.I have everything I need. Here is my plan and the changes.

## 1. Review & Understand the Task
- **Objective:** let the file explorer move **one or several** selected files/folders to another existing folder.
- **Where:** `src/components/filebrowser/*` (explorer UI + context menu) and `src/api/modules/files.js` (API layer).
- **Constraint discovered:** no dedicated `move` endpoint exists on the client; `POST /api/files/rename` (already used by the explorer) takes `{ old_path, new_path }`, so a move is a rename to a new parent folder. Reusing it needs no backend change and already invalidates the path cache.
- **Acceptance:** select N entries → context menu **Move to…** → folder picker dialog → entries land in the target folder; internal drag & drop onto a folder/blank area moves too; illegal targets (into itself, same folder, duplicate names) are blocked.

## 2. Information Gathering (from the codebase)
| Element | Finding |
|---|---|
| `FileExplorer.vue` | Already has upload / create / rename / delete, multi-select (`selectedEntries`), internal `draggable` rows and folder drop zones. Drag handlers ignore internal drags today (`if (this.draggedEntry …) return`). |
| `ContextMenu.vue` | Emits `upload`, `create`, `rename`, `delete`; has props `hasSelection`, `isMultiSelect`, `selectionCount`. |
| `api/modules/files.js` | Has `rename(oldPath, newPath)` → `POST /api/files/rename` with cache invalidation for both paths. `normalizePath` is already imported. |
| Path convention | Entries carry `file_path` (project‑relative, leading `/`, e.g. `/src/a.js`); rename is called with that same convention. |
| Bug noticed | Entry drop zones use `@drop.prevent` **without** `.stop`, so an OS drop on a subfolder bubbles and uploads twice. Fixed along the way for the internal move to be reliable. |

## 3. Changes Summary
| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/api/modules/files.js` | New `move(paths, targetDir)` — moves one or many paths by renaming each to `<target>/<basename>` (inherits cache invalidation). |
| `src/components/filebrowser/MoveDialog.vue` | **New** folder-picker modal: breadcrumbs, subfolder list, up-navigation, destination preview, self-move guard, loading/error states. |
| `src/components/filebrowser/ContextMenu.vue` | New **Move to…** action + `move` emit. |
| `src/components/filebrowser/FileExplorer.vue` | Wires `Move to…` and internal drag & drop to a shared `moveEntries()` (filters no-op/illegal moves, duplicate-name guard, notification, refresh); drop handlers stop propagation. |

## 4. The Changes

