## Behaviour

| Interaction | Result |
|---|---|
| Right-click 1..n selected entries → **Move to…** | `MoveDialog` opens with the folder picker (`Move 3 items`, destination `/lib`) |
| Navigate / breadcrumb / up / refresh inside the dialog | Lists subfolders of the browsed directory only |
| Folder moved into itself or a descendant | Warning + **Move here** disabled |
| Drag entries onto a folder row | Moves them (multi-select aware); row highlights, `dropEffect: move` |
| Drag entries onto the empty area | Moves them into the folder currently viewed |
| Drop already inside the same folder / duplicate name in target | Filtered out locally (no request) / explicit error banner |
| After a move | Notification, selection cleared, listing refreshed, `files:read` + `files:diff` cache invalidated for source **and** destination |

## Notes

- **No backend change:** `move()` reuses `POST /api/files/rename` (`old_path` → `new_path` inside another folder), so it inherits the already-fixed `FileManager.get_file_path()` idempotency for absolute paths.
- **Drop propagation fixed:** entry rows now use `@dragover.stop.prevent` / `@drop.stop.prevent`. Previously an entry drop bubbled to the container and was handled twice (double upload); without `.stop` the new internal move would also run twice.
- `onDragOver` no longer returns early on internal drags, so the container highlights for moves as well as for OS drops.

